#
# Declarative example-conformance fixtures for the learning slice — the test-DSL
# twin of the SHACL pytest in tests/test_learning.py ("this Teaching must
# validate, that counter-example must be rejected"). The harness
# (crates/slicetest run_conformance_cell) validates learning/module.ttl + the one
# bound gmeow:exampleFile against learning/shapes.ttl (gmeow:TeachingShape) and
# compares finding codes.
#
# MESSAGE→CODE shift: the original pytest asserted a specific sh:message substring;
# these cells pin the constraint-component CODE (shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>).
# This is the lossy shift the concepts/epistemics exemplars accepted: the code form
# COLLAPSES distinct sh:message strings that share a constraint component. Because
# each counter-example is a SEPARATE fixture isolating ONE violation, the
# (fixture, code) pair still pins the specific constraint faithfully.
#
# CODE VERIFICATION. Every expectedViolationCode below is pinned to the sh:sourceShape
# it must come from (gmeow:expectedSourceShape), which the harness enforces — a fixture
# that reds a DIFFERENT rule of the same component no longer passes.
#
# WHY NEITHER CELL DECLARES gmeow:expectedSoleFinding. Both used to claim "and NO other
# finding". Measured against the harness, both are false, and for one structural reason:
# this slice has not finished migrating, so it still ships a residual hand-authored
# shapes.ttl (gmeow:TeachingShape) ALONGSIDE the derived gmeow:Teaching-shape and the
# derived gmeow:TeachingSelfTeachConstraintProceduralConstraintShape the pipeline projects
# from the same module axioms. One defect is therefore reported TWICE, by two
# sh:sourceShapes — which is what soleness measures, and it counts two authorities as two
# even when they say the same thing. The duplication is the defect, not the fixtures:
# soleness becomes declarable here the moment the residual shapes.ttl is retired.
#
# The conforming fixture lives under tests/conformance-fixtures/ (NOT examples/)
# and the counter-examples under tests/counter-examples/, so the global
# `make validate` gate never loads them as data; they are validated SLICE-SCOPED
# only (module + slice shapes), intentional and mirroring the concepts precedent.
#
# See dsl/tests/MIGRATION-LEDGER.md for the per-test pytest→DSL mapping.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/learning/tests/> .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed Teaching -------------------------------------
ex:ecTeachingConforms a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/teaching-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture supplies exactly one gmeow:teacher (a gmeow:Agent), one distinct gmeow:learner (a gmeow:Agent), and a gmeow:subjectTaught, so it satisfies gmeow:TeachingShape and validates with no findings. Mirrors test_wellformed_teaching_conforms." .

# --- Violating: teacher equals learner (an agent cannot teach itself) --------
ex:ecTeachingSelf a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/teaching-self.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:TeachingSelfTeachConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's gmeow:teacher and gmeow:learner are the same agent (ex:alice). gmeow:TeachingShape's sh:sparql constraint forbids teacher = learner, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:TeachingSelfTeachConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The residual gmeow:TeachingShape carries a hand-authored twin of the same sh:sparql rule and reports it a second time, so the cell does not declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding (see the header note). Mirrors test_teacher_equals_learner_is_flagged." .

# --- Violating: learner is not a gmeow:Agent --------------------------------
ex:ecTeachingNonAgentLearner a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/teaching-non-agent-learner.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.ClassConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:Teaching-shape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's gmeow:learner (ex:tool) is a gmeow:Artifact, not a gmeow:Agent. The learner property shape carries sh:class gmeow:Agent, so validation MUST emit shacl.ClassConstraintComponent from gmeow:Teaching-shape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The residual gmeow:TeachingShape reports the same class violation a second time, and the derived shape additionally reports shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent because a non-Agent value cannot satisfy the qualified learner restriction; the cell therefore does not declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding (see the header note). Mirrors test_non_agent_learner_is_flagged." .
